    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-5308",
      "problem": "Plot the graph of $y=f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x-1}+2.$",
      "worked_solution": "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $\\color{red}-1$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $1$ unit to the *right*, and\n\n- the $\\color{blue}+2$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $2$ units *up*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242844/assets/fea5a705657b22621f3eb5ffe40cfcd59aef11036674d47e6d1f72e301d531f3.png)",
